	<Device type="custom" id="hkButtons">
		<Name>HomeKit Buttons</Name>
		<ConfigUI>
			<Field id="buttonsIntro" type="label" fontSize="small">
				<Label>Lets Indigo start things in the Home app. This device does nothing in Indigo itself: it appears in the Home app as a button accessory (like a wireless remote), and the Home app decides what each press does.

Use it to reach what only the Home app controls (Matter or Apple-only devices, HomePod music, Home scenes) from any Indigo trigger, schedule, action group or Control Page.

1. Choose the buttons, their names, the bridge to publish them to and their HomeKit name.
2. In the Home app, open the new accessory: each button has a single, double and long press. Choose what each one runs.
3. In Indigo, press a button with the action "Press a HomeKit Button" (HomeKitLink Siri actions).

A physical remote or wall switch can be passed on to the Home app too: see the wiki (Supported Devices > HomeKit Buttons).

The other direction (the Home app running something in Indigo) is not this device: publish an action group or device as a switch instead.

Changing the number of buttons or their names restarts its bridge.</Label>
			</Field>
			<Field id="buttonCount" type="menu" defaultValue="1">
				<Label>Buttons:</Label>
				<List>
					<Option value="1">1</Option>
					<Option value="2">2</Option>
					<Option value="3">3</Option>
					<Option value="4">4</Option>
					<Option value="5">5</Option>
					<Option value="6">6</Option>
					<Option value="7">7</Option>
					<Option value="8">8</Option>
					<Option value="9">9</Option>
					<Option value="10">10</Option>
				</List>
			</Field>
			<Field id="buttonNames" type="textfield" defaultValue="">
