	<Device type="custom" id="hksvRecorder">
		<Name>HomeKit Secure Video Recorder</Name>
		<ConfigUI>
			<Field id="hksvIntro" type="label" fontSize="small">
				<Label>Adds HomeKit Secure Video to one HomeKitLink camera. Home hubs then record its motion (and doorbell) events to iCloud, as set in the Home app. Needs an iCloud+ plan and a home hub (Apple TV or HomePod).

While the Home app allows recording, one ffmpeg keeps the last few seconds of the camera in memory (HomeKit wants recordings to start just before the motion). If one of the camera's streams suits HomeKit it is copied, which uses almost no CPU; otherwise it is re-encoded. The device's states show which, and the ffmpeg's CPU and memory.

Saving restarts the camera's bridge to add the recording services. Disabling this device stops recording but keeps the camera's Home app settings; deleting it removes them.</Label>
			</Field>
			<Field id="cameraDeviceId" type="menu" defaultValue="">
				<Label>Camera:</Label>
				<List class="self" method="hksv_camera_list" dynamicReload="true"/>
			</Field>
			<Field id="hksvCameraNote" type="label" fontSize="small" alignWithControl="true">
				<Label>Cameras published to HomeKit by HomeKitLink (BlueIris, SecuritySpy or UniFi Protect). The camera needs its motion sensor turned on in HomeKitLink.</Label>
			</Field>
			<Field id="hksvAllowCopy" type="checkbox" defaultValue="true">
				<Label>Copy a suitable stream:</Label>
				<Description>Record without re-encoding when a stream suits HomeKit</Description>
			</Field>
			<Field id="hksvDoorbellExtends" type="checkbox" defaultValue="true">
				<Label>Doorbell presses:</Label>
				<Description>Keep a recording going for 30 s after a press</Description>
			</Field>
			<Field id="hksvEncoder" type="menu" defaultValue="h264_videotoolbox">
				<Label>When re-encoding, use:</Label>
				<List>
					<Option value="h264_videotoolbox">VideoToolbox (Mac hardware, low CPU)</Option>
					<Option value="libx264">libx264 (software, high CPU)</Option>
				</List>
			</Field>
		</ConfigUI>
